---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "Can LKProfessionals perform a security review of an existing system?",
    answer:
      "Yes. The review scope can include websites, applications, servers, access controls, dependencies, backup arrangements and relevant configuration depending on the environment.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Does a security audit guarantee that a system cannot be compromised?",
    answer:
      "No. Security work reduces identifiable risk but cannot provide an absolute guarantee against every future vulnerability, attack or operational failure.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can you secure a website developed by another provider?",
    answer:
      "Potentially, yes. We first need appropriate access and an understanding of the platform, hosting environment, codebase and current technical condition.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Do backups count as cybersecurity?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Reliable backup and recovery are an important part of resilience because incidents, mistakes, corruption and infrastructure failures can all affect availability or data.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "What is security hardening?",
    answer:
      "Hardening reduces unnecessary exposure by disabling unused services, tightening permissions, improving configurations and strengthening the environment around the application or server.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Does security need ongoing maintenance?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Software, infrastructure, access, dependencies and threats change over time, so security cannot be treated as a one-time configuration exercise.",
  },
];
---

<section class="security-faq">
  <div class="site-container security-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>Cybersecurity FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions before strengthening the environment.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="security-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .security-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .security-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(16rem, 0.68fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .security-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .security-faq h2 {
    max-width: 11ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .security-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .security-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .security-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .security-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .security-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
